  volume      =  34,
  number      =  6,
  pages       = "1130--1143",
  abstract    = "G-formula is a popular approach for estimating the effects of
                 time-varying treatments or exposures from longitudinal data.
                 G-formula is typically implemented using Monte-Carlo
                 simulation, with non-parametric bootstrapping used for
                 inference. In longitudinal data settings missing data are a
                 common issue, which are often handled using multiple
                 imputation, but it is unclear how G-formula and multiple
                 imputation should be combined. We show how G-formula can be
