  volume    =  65,
  number    =  9,
  pages     = "746--750",
  abstract  = "This essay argues that work, and the socioeconomic class
               polarities it creates, plays a fundamental role in determining
               inequalities in the distribution of morbidity and mortality. This
               is by means of uneven exposure to physical hazards and
               psychosocial risks in the workplace, as well as by inequalities
               in exclusion from the labour market and the absence of paid work.
