  number    =  5,
  pages     = "1656--1661",
  abstract  = "Recent methodological innovation is giving rise to an increasing
               number of applied papers in medical and epidemiological journals
               in which natural direct and indirect effects are estimated.
               However, there is a longstanding debate on whether such effects
               are relevant targets of inference in population health. In light
               of the repeated calls for a more pragmatic and consequential
               epidemiology, we review three issues often raised in this debate:
